Z||000002||MikeSchaefer||06-22-2001||01:03 AM||||I really like the looks of the Power Acoustic "Fire and Ice" amps, they are pretty powerful and look great.  I don't know how great of quality they are though, anyone know?<BR>Mike||||reg||2
Z||000003||sjp777||06-22-2001||01:04 AM||||A 5 channel amp will be spendy and probably not the best way to go.<P>It would be better to give the sub its own amp. Look for a 200w amp that you can bridge to mono to drive the sub.<P>If you need more power to the other speakers, then go for a 4 channel for them<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||06-22-2001||02:43 AM||||I agree with sjp777, It is better to have a 4-channel for the mains and a seperate one for the subs. <P>Go to:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/default.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.onlinecarstereo.com/caraudio/default.asp</A> <P>For great deals.<P>Pioneer GMX 552 150W bridged $119<BR>Pioneer GMX 354 35W X 4  $139<BR>OR<BR>Alpine T406 240W bridged $139<BR>Alpine F200 75W X 4  $169<BR>OR<BR>Rockford Fosgate Punch 120A2 120W bridged $149<BR>Rockford Fosgate Punch 400.4 50W X 4 $260<P>They don't carry Eclipse but the MTX was $409.<P><BR>Hope this Helps.<P>P.S. The shifter still works GREAT!<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000005||KRMFiero||06-22-2001||09:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MikeSchaefer:<BR><B>I really like the looks of the Power Acoustic "Fire and Ice" amps, they are pretty powerful and look great.  I don't know how great of quality they are though, anyone know?<BR>Mike</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No offence but they are a waste of money, junk<P>I would go with the MTX, they are great amps<BR>kyle||||reg||1
