Z||000007||sqoach||06-22-2001||11:18 AM||||I agree with Kyle. MTX amps are under-rated. I have a Blue Thunder 50x2 that is actually pushing 62x2. They are shipped from the factory showing the actual specs. They are a very good quality amp, IMO. And I found mine for a pretty good deal on eBay.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||14
Z||000008||Tom88gt||06-22-2001||11:44 AM||||I'm cheap.  I just bought a "Phase Linear" amp from a local electronics/appliance store for $49 bucks.  It has a sub crossover (HZ unknown) and is bridgable to mono.  It claims to be a 200 watt amp with 125 watts rms bridged.  It uses a 20 amp fuse so the numbers are not too unbelievable...watts = 20 amps X 12 volts...cut this number in half to estimate the amp's inefficiency.  Yes, its a cheap made in China amp.  But my main speakers are powered right of the head unit with only 20 watts rms per channel.  Plus the amp is small enough to fit under the dash, I just made a mounting plate that fit right under the AC housing.  I have a 6.5 Bazooka Tude behind the passenger seat and it is loud, deep and clear!!!||||reg||14
Z||000009||Seanh||06-22-2001||12:46 PM||||Stay away from Power Acustic amps, they are over-rated, and poor quality. I do like the looks of them though.<P>MTX amps are definatly under-rated, by a lot. I blew 2 15" Orion's with an MTX rated at 500w RMS, I bet it was pushing close to 650w RMS or more at 14.4v. I would also agree with the majority here and say you should get 2 seperate amps. Iv found that most all of the 5 channels don't put out enough power for a subwoofer to fit my taste's. Depends on what sub your going to use, its voice coil configuration, RMS power handling, etc..<P>Amp brands I would reccomend are Kenwood eXcelon, MMats, Candance, MTX, Rockford, JBL, JL, EarthQuake, Lightning Audio, Orion, PPI, US Amps, Xtant, and Zapco. All those brands are high quality, good customer service, durable, pretty much all around the best amps you could get. If you have any questions on one in particular, post about it and I'm sure everyone will give you their opinion on its quality.||||reg||1
Z||000010||fierodude||06-22-2001||12:51 PM||||could someone tell me what watt my amp is or what this means 45w\2<P>------------------<BR>slice the rice! it dosen't pay to drive jap - crap!||||reg||1
Z||000011||sjp777||06-22-2001||01:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tom88gt:<BR><B>I'm cheap.  I just bought a "Phase Linear" amp from a local electronics/appliance store for $49 bucks.  It has a sub crossover (HZ unknown) and is bridgable to mono.  It claims to be a 200 watt amp with 125 watts rms bridged.  It uses a 20 amp fuse so the numbers are not too unbelievable...watts = 20 amps X 12 volts...cut this number in half to estimate the amp's inefficiency.  Yes, its a cheap made in China amp.  But my main speakers are powered right of the head unit with only 20 watts rms per channel.  Plus the amp is small enough to fit under the dash, I just made a mounting plate that fit right under the AC housing.  I have a 6.5 Bazooka Tude behind the passenger seat and it is loud, deep and clear!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Be careful, I have that same amp bridged to mono and driving a 8" punch xlc. Just last week I must have blown half of it 'cause now it only works in stereo mode, not bridged and I only get half the bass I used to.<P>It's about to get yanked and tossed.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_4.jpg"> <BR>88GT 5sp, in desperate need of an LT1<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||13
Z||000012||Maniak84||06-22-2001||04:12 PM||||I also have one of those Phase Linears. I had tried it hooked to one of the Bazooka tubes for a while before I broke bown and made my footwell sub. It really didn't make me happ with the results. Now its hooked u to my dash speakers and it does fine for that. I have a 400w amp to the sub now. Much happier.<P>Hey seanh, does Zapco still make eqs? I have a friend with one in his truck and it i a slick unit and would mount nicely over the dome light pod, but I can't ever find one.<BR>(edit- oops, this is stimpy, btw.)<p>[This message has been edited by Maniak84 (edited 06-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||Seanh||06-22-2001||04:47 PM||||Yeah, Zapco still makes some damn nice EQ's. They show them all on their website <A HREF="http://www.zapco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zapco.com</A>  , under "products", then "processors". I am sure there is a place on the net that sells them too, I'll check when I have a chance.||||reg||1
Z||000014||V8Dreamer||06-22-2001||05:03 PM||||I'd definately go with two seperate amps, that way you can go with a cheaper one for the sub too, since the quality isn't quite as important there, just dont' go toooo cheap.  For the rest of the speakers you can get a 50x4 or something, just make sure the speakers can take it and also make sure the wattage is in RMS, peak doesn't mean s&*t.<P>Ryan||||reg||1
Z||000015||RDosdorian||06-22-2001||05:34 PM||||Get an amp with CLEAN power output.  You don't want the distortion and the way the amp looks (the shell color) does nothing for the performance.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Seanh||06-22-2001||05:57 PM||||Most good name brand amps are rated in RMS, but some may be in Peak/MAX. Its a good rule of thumb to assume RMS is about 50% of peak, its usally less, or sometimes more depending on the class of amp you have.||||reg||1
Z||000017||varnster||06-22-2001||06:35 PM||||I have a 4x100 and a 1x150 powering my gear.<BR>both are sony xplode both have been in use for about 3 years with wonderful service!<BR>If you want to impress the guys at the sound<BR>shop you can spend alot of cash, but if its for YOU wanting good affordable sound I highly recomend this line of amp, but im sure their are alot of guys here on the forum that dont agree, and are good friends<BR>with the guys at the sound shop and their cash regester. in my book these amps are highly underated. ||||reg||1
